          {
            title: 'Teka',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Teka is a four-player partnership trick-taking game from Afghanistan. 52 cards, 13 each. First to 104 points wins. Ace high to 2 low. Bidding: pass, ter, behi ter, or 8â€“13 tricks (or Double 13â€”win all tricks solo). Highest bidder is declarer, chooses trump, leads first trick with a trump. Follow suit; else any card. Declarer scores tricks won; Double 13 scores 26 or 52 to opponents if lost. New deal if a hand has no card above 10.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: Afghanistan\nTime Period: Early 1900s\nHistorical Development: The game evolved from traditional card games in the region and is the most popular social game in Afghanistan.\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 6\nOptimal Players: 4\nPartnerships: Optional',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Type: Standard 52-card deck\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck\nScore sheet (optional)\nTable space',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Cards per Player: 13 each (all at once)\nDealing Pattern: Counterclockwise\nPlayer to dealer's left cuts before the deal. Cards shuffled only before first deal; later dealers may cut but not shuffle.",
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
